THE RITUAL - AS EXPERIENCED:
"The Preparation:
Three Highlord priests - I never learned their names, they wore ceremonial masks. They spent days preparing the ritual chamber. Circles within circles, written in silver dragon blood. The irony was not lost on any of us."
"They had a prisoner: Silvara's clutchmate, a young silver dragon named Gwyneth. She knew what was coming. We all did."
Khisanth's voice becomes hollow. "They kept us separate - five dragons in five chambers, arranged in a pentagram around the central ritual space. We could hear each other roar, but couldn't help."

"The Forging:
The priests began at midnight. They chanted in three languages simultaneously - Common for the mortal world, Draconic to bind us, and Abyssal for the demonic power source."
"Gwyneth was brought to the center. They... killed her slowly. Ritually. Each part of her essence was woven into the Crown's creation. Her blood became the binding agent. Her scales became the Crown's structure. Her final scream became the enchantment that would compel obedience."
She pauses, old rage and grief mixing. "It took six hours. Six hours of listening to her die, knowing her death would enslave us."

"The Binding Moment:
When the Crown was complete, they placed it on the Highlord's head - I believe it was Verminaard, but the Dark Queen herself was present in spectral form, so details blur."
"The moment the Crown touched mortal brow, I FELT it. Like hooks sinking into my very essence. Not my body - my SELF. The core of what makes me... me."
Her claws scrape stone unconsciously. "I could still think. Still feel. Still hate. But I could not CHOOSE. When the Crown commanded, I obeyed. My body moved without my will. My breath weapon fired at targets I didn't want to kill. My mind screamed inside a prison of my own flesh."

"The Binding Mechanics:
What you need to understand: the Crown doesn't work like a simple domination spell. It's a CONTRACT made flesh. Each dragon bound to it had our true names woven into the ritual. Our essences became... co-signers of a pact we never agreed to."
"The Crown holder could invoke our names through the artifact, and we were compelled to serve as if we'd sworn oaths to Takhisis herself. Breaking those commands felt like fighting against reality itself."

"The Weakness:
But here's what the priests didn't fully understand: they built it using DRAGON sacrifice. Draconic magic has rules - older than gods, older than demons. You cannot bind what is not given."
"Gwyneth died unwillingly. Her essence was FORCED into the Crown's creation. That created... instability. Microscopic, but real. The binding held because Takhisis's divine power reinforced it, but the foundation was flawed."
"When Takhisis fell, when her power withdrew? That flaw became exploitable. The Crown still worked, but it could be resisted with enough will. Eventually, it could be BROKEN."
She looks at Johannes directly. "You sabotaged the Highlord ritual. That final break severed Takhisis's reinforcement completely. The Crown still EXISTS, but its divine backing is gone. Right now, it's operating on momentum - the binding magic persists, but it's weakening daily."

